This is an idea I've got:
 
One boring part of nethack is that on the way down, I sometimes
encoutner levels with almost no monsters/items at all. Personally, I
think that this makes the game dull, I would like to have more action.
I also think that 50 levels is to much, it takes much to long time to 
complete a game. The 20 lowest levels is only a search for the amulet
requiring nothing but patience (and heat resistance).

My "cure" for that is for each level to contain more rooms. The
current version doesn't allow more rooms than are visible on the
screen at the same time. By letting new rooms be generated as the
player "exits" the screen into a new part of the level, this
(wonderful) game could be played at a much larger playground. A
player could of course get seriously lost in a game like this. I
also think that it should be tougher to survive in the outer
regions of a level.

By limiting the game to, say 20 levels (or less), entering a new 
level could/would require much more skill than it does now.

As a result of the above suggestions, the game could now be played
in two ways. One could try to get through the game with as little
points as possible (easier to "avoid" points, making it harder to
complete). But if you want to score really high and collect lots
of wands/potions/gems/scrollbooks etc the opportunities would now
be virtually unlimited.

I know that theese ways of playing already exist. My remedy makes
it possible to play them in a much cleaner way. For example: if 
you're trying to collect lots of items a good way now would be to
save your game, entering the new level, play around a bit, and then 
decide if it's good enough to keep. If not, quit the game you're
playing, and continue to play on a copy of your old game.


